drysdall@waikato.ac.nz writes:

>found a wand, engraved with it and got the message: "What do you wish for?"

>My first wish was for bGDSM since everybody says this is pretty cool.

Actually you should always use your first wish for "3 blessed scrolls of
charging" whenever you find a wand of wishing. That way you will have at
least 3 more wishes when the wand for the first time says "Nothing happens".

Besides, gray dragon scale mail is better than black, because it gives you
magic resistance.

>But then I had to write something. So I just entered nothing and received the
>message "The wand of wishing glows and then fades." or something like that. My
>question is, did the wand of wishing use up another charge when I wrote? or did
>it just use up one when I received the bGDSM? (I know it is uncursed)

The wands always use exactly one charge when you either engrave with them or
zap them. No matter if you actually write something or just press enter.
And some wands, like the wand of wishing, give the whole zapping effect
when you engrave with them, but still they use exactly one charge.

>I know that I have at least one (charge zero) wish left. What should I do?

>should I risk trying for some scrolls of charging? Whenever I have tried
>recharging a WoW in 3.0i with a scroll of charging, it always died on me. Does
>anybody know roughly what the odds are?

Are you sure the wands you tried to charge weren't already once charged?
You see, you can only charge a wand once. And if you use the "charge zero",
you can never charge that wand again. Therefore, you should only try to use
the zero charge from the wand of wishing only after it has been charged.

>Also, if I do decide to wish for a weapon, how do I word it? Is it:
> The {blessed} {weapon name}

Yes, that works. But it is better to wish for 
blessed +3 rustproof (weapon name).
(You don't have to write the "the"..)


